  "details": "The current supported endpoints in https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/osc-as-input-controller currently describe gamepad-like inputs, but also happen to cover a reasonable amount of the keyboard+mouse inputs, with the exception of driving left and right hand gestures, and consequently, facial expressions.\n\nConcretely, the ask is to add left-hand and right-hand gestures analogous to {l,r}shift-f1 through {l,r}shift-f8.\n\nThere are a couple of reasons to do this:\n\n  1 Simplifying input handling\n\nVRChat's support of legacy SteamVR input won't last forever, and updating will very likely carry the baggage of an overhaul of the input action bindings. VR controls as a whole have moved towards what can roughly described as a Oculus Touch-compatible model. \n\nVive Controllers are still supported by HTC yet also very difficult to support, but even so, are also useful for having the only reliable expression selector.\n\nAdding OSC Expressions support will allow the input system to reduce its support surface significantly without significant loss of functionality, especially if the creator community can provide their own emulation to support and fill in a loss of native Vive Controller expression support as it currently exists.\n\n  2 Accessibility\n\nFor the same reasons that the rest of the OSC input controls help with accessibility, this would help achieve parity with other inputs.\n\n  3 Scriptability\n\nWho wouldn't want a program to assist them in triggering ninjutsu hand seals before they do a Naruto run animation?",
